To detect that this is an update to an existing item, we can define a "canBe" function that checks whether the item's "id" attribute matches an existing item in the balance:
```python
function canBe(item, existingItem) {
  return item.id === existingItem.id;
}
```
When updating the balance with the new item, we can iterate over the existing items in the balance and apply the "canBe" function to determine whether to update an existing item or append a new item. Here is an example implementation:
```javascript
function updateBalance(balance, newItem, canBe) {
  let updated = false;

  const updatedBalance = balance.map(existingItem => {
    if (canBe(newItem, existingItem)) {
      updated = true;
      return { ...existingItem, ...newItem };
    } else {
      return existingItem;
    }
  });

  if (!updated) {
    updatedBalance.push(newItem);
  }

  return updatedBalance;
}
```
