2. Define the Fields: Next, you need to define the fields that will be included in the entity. You can do this by adding a code block inside the view definition. For example:
```yaml
view: my_entity {
  description: "My entity description"
  sql_table_name: my_entity_table
  dimension: id {
    type: number
    sql: ${TABLE}.id ;;
  }
  dimension: name {
    type: string
    sql: ${TABLE}.name ;;
  }
}
```
In this example, we define two dimensions: "id" and "name". The "type" parameter specifies the data type of the field, and the "sql" parameter specifies the SQL statement that retrieves the data for that field.

