This will override the `console.log` function with a new function that performs the custom behavior before calling the original `console.log` function using the `apply` method. The `...args` syntax allows you to pass any number of arguments to the function, and the `apply` method allows you to specify the `this` value for the function and pass an array of arguments.

You can then use `console.log` as you normally would, and the custom behavior will be executed before the log message is printed to the console.

